## **3.4  Digital Lead CPD Pathway**

Every Digital Lead follows a structured CPD pathway. The pathway is differentiated by RAG rating so that support matches actual need. All resources are free to access via institutional licensing or open-access tiers.

**Platforms:**

- Microsoft Learn — free, self-paced, certification-linked. Recommended for Teams, Accessibility, Copilot, and Productivity modules.

- Jisc — staff digital development pathways aligned to the Digital Teaching Professional Framework (DTPF). Covers digital pedagogy, data literacy, online safety, and digital identity.

- LinkedIn Learning — available where institutional licence exists. Broad coverage across all digital skills areas.

### **Phase 1: Digital Foundations (All Digital Leads — Term 3, April–June 2026)**

Minimum expectation for every named Digital Lead before the end of the academic year.

| **When** | **Focus** | **Platform / Resource** | **Outcome / Evidence** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| April–May 2026 | Teams environment fundamentals: channels, naming conventions, Assignments, accessibility settings | Microsoft Learn: "Collaborate with Teams" | Completion badge logged in DPC tracker. Health Check run in own area. |
| April–May 2026 | Accessibility by Design: Accessibility Checker, alt text, captions, heading styles | Microsoft Learn: "Create accessible content with Microsoft 365" | Completion badge. At least one resource audit completed in own area. |
| May–June 2026 | Digital inclusion awareness: WCAG 2.2 AA principles, assistive technology overview | Jisc: "Developing your digital literacies" (Modules 1–2) | Module completion logged. Shared one accessibility tip at team meeting. |
| June 2026 | Digital Lead induction session with DPC | Facilitated by Graeme Wright — 90 mins, in person or Teams | Attendance. Health Check completed and results shared with HoA. |

### **Phase 2: Digital Inclusion (Term 1–2, September 2026–January 2027)**

Building on Foundations — differentiated by RAG. Leads at RAG 1–2 may move directly to Phase 3.

| **When** | **Focus** | **Platform / Resource** | **Outcome / Evidence** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Sept–Oct 2026 | Digital pedagogy: active learning, formative assessment, student-facing Teams use | Jisc: "Learning and Teaching" strand (Modules 3–5) | Module completion. One Teach Meet contribution or coaching log entry. |
| Oct–Nov 2026 | AI in education: ethical use, prompt literacy, FE-specific guidance | Microsoft Learn: "AI Fundamentals" + DPC-curated AI briefing | AI module badge. Written reflection submitted to DPC (one paragraph). |
| Nov–Dec 2026 | Data and evidence: using Teams Analytics, ProMonitor integration, learning walk data | Microsoft Learn: "Excel / Forms for data" + DPC coaching session | One data-informed intervention documented in team notes. |
| Jan 2027 | Digital Lead peer review — share practice with one other Digital Lead | DPC-facilitated network session (Teams or in person) | Peer review log completed. Good practice shared with DPC for wider circulation. |

### **Phase 3: Digital Innovation (Term 3 2026–27 and beyond)**

For Digital Leads at RAG 1–2 and those who have completed Phases 1 and 2. This phase is about leading change, not just embedding practice.

| **When** | **Focus** | **Platform / Resource** | **Outcome / Evidence** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Feb–April 2027 | Leading digital change: influencing culture, running CPD for peers | LinkedIn Learning: "Leading Digital Transformation" or equivalent | One peer CPD session delivered. Documented in DPC evidence log. |
| April 2027 | Specialist digital skills mapping in curriculum area (with HoA) | Area-specific tools + DPC coaching | Specialist digital skills map completed and signed off by HoA. |
| Ongoing | External network engagement: Jisc community, DigiWest, sector events | Jisc community of practice / DigiWest network | Attendance or contribution logged termly. |
| July 2027 | Governance Review 2 contribution: Digital Lead impact report | DPC-facilitated — input from Leads to annual review | Written contribution (100 words) submitted to DPC for governance report. |

